# Git
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Documentation
# NOTE on the pattern below: unlike .gitignore, a bare .dockerignore pattern
# with no `/` and no `**` is anchored to the CONTEXT ROOT ONLY -- it does not
# match at every depth (see docs.docker.com/build/building/context/, the
# `**/*.go` example; verified 2026-08-25 against the live docs and against
# github.com/moby/moby#27144). So `*.md` here excludes only README.md /
# CHANGELOG.md / TODO.md etc. at the repo root; it does NOT reach
# crates/*/README.md, which every publishable crate manifest needs present
# via its `readme = "README.md"` key (Cargo metadata tooling such as
# `cargo package`/`cargo publish --dry-run` run inside the build context
# would fail without it). Do not "fix" this to `**/*.md` -- that would
# actually strip every crate README from the build context.
*.md
docs/
LICENSE*

# Tests and benchmarks
# Same root-anchoring rule as above: these three patterns exclude only
# ./benches, ./tests and ./examples at the repo root. crates/*/tests,
# crates/*/benches and crates/*/examples are a separate, unrelated
# directory tree and are NOT covered -- they stay in the build context
# (harmlessly; nothing in the image build reads them).
benches/
tests/
examples/

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
